# PROVENANCE — layout and shared source

Payload provenance is per family, in `<family>/PROVENANCE`. This file covers the
two things that are not per family, and the rule that decides which level
anything belongs at.

## The family is the top-level key

Every artifact here is chip-coupled: the prebuilt MI modules are built for one
chip, the sensor drivers differ per family under identical filenames, and the
ISP and VENC blobs are per chip in the vendor's own tree. So the family is the
outermost directory and each family is self-contained.

This replaces a layout keyed by kernel release first. That level asserted a
property of the *kernel* about payload that is a property of the *chip*, and it
let two mistakes in that the current shape makes unrepresentable:

  - infinity6c sensor drivers filed under `4.9.84/` when Infinity6C is a 5.10.61
    family. That family now carries its own 5.10.61 payload beside the two
    4.9.84 ones, which is exactly what the old level could not express.
  - one `kmod-` directory outside any family, so `sigmastar-sdk.mk` resolved it
    without `$(SOC_FAMILY)` and an Infinity6B0 build would have installed
    Infinity6E's MI modules. Same-chip only by luck of there being one family.

The kernel release did not disappear -- it moved into the kmod directory name,
which is the one place a mismatch is fatal and undetectable. See the family
files for why.

## sensor-src-common/

`Makefile` and `sensor_config.c`, which every family's `sensor-src/` symlinks to
as `../../sensor-src-common/`. Upstream keeps them one level above the families
and the families symlink up; that arrangement is preserved, just at a path that
survives the families being hoisted.

Both are upstream's verbatim, including a `SIGMASTAR_MARUKO` branch for
infinity6c that is now dead. Left alone so the file still diffs cleanly against
upstream.

## Sensor drivers, all families

From openipc/sensors @ 8143e4da181d39d569572519595ce4b7e1a9a02d, sigmastar half
only; the hisilicon half (916K) is not carried. Source, compiled at build time
against the pinned kernel.

These are **not** vendor dumps. The vendor SDK has 68 drivers; OpenIPC ships 11
per family, renamed and reformatted, and the overlap has diverged -- gc4653, the
one this board uses, is retuned from 25fps to 30fps (Preview_MAX_FPS 25->30,
vts_25fps->vts_30fps, Preview_line_period 26667->22222, ENABLE_OTP_DD dropped,
plus register init table edits). Five of the eleven do not exist in the vendor
SDK at all. Re-deriving from the vendor tree would lose sensors and regress the
board to 25fps.

No flavour key, deliberately: `drv_sensor.h` is byte-identical between vendor
releases 0601 and 0902, and the built driver's only coupling to the vendor
bundle is four symbols -- CamOsMemAlloc, CamOsMemRelease, CamOsPrintf,
CamOsUsSleep -- all exported by mhal.ko. Kernel-coupled, not release-coupled.

Per family because the same filename is a different driver in each. Between
infinity6e and infinity6b0, `sensor_imx335_mipi.c` differs by 1434 lines,
`sensor_imx307_mipi.c` by 777 and `sensor_gc2053_mipi.c` by 10;
`drv_ms_cus_sensor.h` differs too. Only `sensor_gc4653_mipi.c` is identical.
`drv_sensor.h` happens to match between those two, so it is not what the split
rests on -- the drivers are. It does differ for infinity6c, by 15 lines, and
that family alone carries `sensor_spi_api.h`.

The family also selects which drivers exist at all: 11 for infinity6e, 18 for
infinity6b0, 10 for infinity6c. Where a driver genuinely is shared, upstream
symlinks rather than copies -- infinity6c takes imx335 and imx415 from
infinity6e that way, and those links are preserved here.

`sigmastar-sdk.mk` builds `$(SOC_FAMILY)/sensor-src`, and `soc/sigmastar/*.mk`
defines infinity6e and infinity6b0. infinity6c is carried without a target, for
a port that the Raptor i6c backend needs the userspace half of; its drivers were
removed in 4b08ea4 while the family had no payload and restored once it did.
infinity6c symlinks imx335 and imx415 across to infinity6e, so the two families
cannot be separated.

Upstream also ships infinity6, which nothing here needs; restore it from the
hash above if a target appears.

## Case

Lowercase, matching `SOC_FAMILY` in `soc/sigmastar/*.mk` literally, so the
packages index this tree with `$(SOC_FAMILY)` and no case conversion.
johnchia/sigmastar-lib uses the same spelling for the same reason.
